meta {
  name: Get Channel Settings
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/communication/channel-settings
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Read the business's messaging channel capability + per-feature overrides for the
  active scope (tenant default when the JWT has no active branch, else that branch).
  Tenant + branch come from the JWT — never the body (CLAUDE.md §4.7).

  These flags/overrides gate which channels AUTOMATIC notifications actually send
  over (`NotificationEnablementService`). When nothing is configured the read
  synthesises defaults — every channel enabled, no overrides — which is exactly the
  backward-compatible behaviour (send over every requested channel).

  ## Response `data`
  - `branchId`: the scope (null = tenant default).
  - `isEmailChannelEnabled` / `isSmsChannelEnabled` / `isWhatsappChannelEnabled`.
  - `overrides[]`: `{ feature, channel, status }` (status `ACTIVE` | `DONT_SEND`).
}
